  "rationale": "Retain the incumbent. The Analyst's own evidence shows that the executing pointcloud scalar contains no pair-kernel, moment, joint-motif or geometry-block term (formula_registry diagnostic_limit), so the strongest reproducible coordinate signals (pair_kernel_1.5/2.5, joint_internal/innovation RMS) cannot be expressed by any permitted edit; they are diagnostic only. The permitted edits are pointcloud_delta_A, region_index, teacher_neighbors, temporal_region_index and temporal_teacher_blend. No supplied evidence establishes a defensible expected affinity advantage for changing pointcloud_delta_A away from the incumbent 1.0 A, for re-pointing region_index to a specific landmark, for changing teacher_neighbors from 4, or for a temporal blend: all 200 continuous rows have extrapolation_allowed false, polynomial_accepted false and method observed_node_linear, with relative_node_RMSE 0.28-0.997 and sign_changes 1-13, so no validated time-conditioned salience exists to justify temporal_region_index or temporal_teacher_blend. The curve_support selected set (24 curves) is not the same as the audited set, so it cannot license a temporal edit. Increment contrasts are mostly non-significant after BH (only increment_effects:14 reaches q<0.05 and its sign opposes the endpoint effect for landmark_00_occupancy3), and the turnover residual is an accounting diagnostic, not a causal selection effect. Temperatures are immutable and no temperature edit is proposed. Because the affinity-first objective is primary and no permitted bounded declarative edit has a defensible expected advantage over the incumbent, retaining the incumbent is the correct choice; the Analyst's hypotheses remain descriptive and are not converted into an operative edit.",
  "role": "Designer"
}
